{"contents":[{"uri":"montagent://schema/def/Keyframedouble.json","mimeType":"application/json","text":"{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "t": {
      "type": "integer",
      "format": "int64",
      "description": "Milliseconds on the project's one absolute clock. Legal outside the element's own\nrange — that is how a trimmed move is spelled, and seven of the fixture's photo\nelements carry one."
    },
    "t_from": {
      "description": "What this record's own `t` was derived from, where the author recorded it\n(ADR-0086).\n\n**Immediately after `t`**, which is the whole of ADR-0086's key-order\nspecification: ADR-0041 derives canonical order from schema order, and schema order\nis this struct's declaration order, so adjacency to the annotated value costs\nnothing to state twice and cannot drift.\n\nOptional, and its absence means *no claim* — never a claim of independence\n(ADR-0086's sixth condition of admission). Required was measured and rejected: on\nthe committed fixture it would put an escape value on 121 instants to check 14.",
      "$ref": "montagent://schema/def/Derivation.json"
    },
    "v": {
      "type": "number",
      "format": "double"
    },
    "ease": {
      "description": "The shape of the interpolation **arriving at** this record from the previous one.\n\nADR-0038: required on every record except the first, where it is a schema error.\nPresence is a pure function of position in the list, so there is never an absent\nvalue to default, normalise, or keep in sync with SPLIT's equality check. The\n`Option` here carries that positional rule, not a default.",
      "$ref": "montagent://schema/def/Ease.json"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "t",
    "v",
    "ease"
  ],
  "description": "One `{\"t\",\"t_from\",\"v\",\"ease\"}` record — `t_from` optional (ADR-0086)."
}
"}]}

