{"contents":[{"uri":"montagent://schema/def/AnimatableVolume.json","mimeType":"application/json","text":"{
  "anyOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "montagent://schema/def/Volume.json",
      "description": "Constant for the element's whole life."
    },
    {
      "type": "array",
      "prefixItems": [
        {
          "$ref": "montagent://schema/def/FirstKeyframeVolume.json"
        }
      ],
      "items": {
        "$ref": "montagent://schema/def/KeyframeVolume.json"
      },
      "description": "Keyframed. Clamps at both ends (ADR-0012): before the first record the value is the\nfirst value, after the last it is the last, so *\"and then it holds\"* costs no syntax.\nRecords must be written with strictly increasing `t` (ADR-0082) — array order is\nclock order.",
      "minItems": 1
    }
  ],
  "description": "A property that is either one value or a list of keyframe records.\n\nThe polymorphism is the format's, not a convenience: ADR-0055 restates it for `volume`\nas *\"the same scalar-or-keyframe-array polymorphism every other animatable property\nalready has.\"* It is deliberately **not** the same as the `scale` union ADR-0012\nrejected — that was two shapes for one *value* (`1.08` versus `[1.08, 1.08]`), which\nputs a shape test in every consumer; this is a value versus its animation over time,\nwhich no amount of normalising can collapse."
}
"}]}

